WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.420
Holy Usopp! What a perfectly juicy chapter to&nbsp;
leave us with for the upcoming 4 week hunger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.120
streak. Oda-sensei really gave us a ton of meat to&nbsp;
chew on while we wait for the story to continue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:19.080
And thank god, we didn't actually end up rushing&nbsp;
out of Wano within two chapters, but will get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:25.200
some more time to wrap things up properly. Let's&nbsp;
begin with the new bounties we have gotten. Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.700
Law and kid all have received an absolutely&nbsp;
ridiculous bounty of 3 BILLION berries, making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:39.600
all three of them more wanted than Blackbeard.&nbsp;
I think this bounty reveal is a big suprise in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.340
a number of ways. I'm sure there many people&nbsp;
who expected it to be a lot higher than this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:51.240
including me. But honestly, I really love&nbsp;
3 Billion for a number of reasons. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.400
you really think about it, it makes a ton&nbsp;
of sense. Putting Luffy above Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:03.720
underlines really nicely how impactful his&nbsp;
victory over Kaido was. Yes Blackbeard killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:10.380
off Whitebeard and taking his devil fruit&nbsp;
shook the world, but Whitebeard was sick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:16.680
old and had already been fighting against&nbsp;
the strongest fighters in the marines. Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:23.520
meanwhile was facing off against a significantly&nbsp;
younger Kaido, still in his prime and known as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.940
most powerful creature in the world. And yes,&nbsp;
Kaido also was fighting against the scabbards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:38.160
Yamato and 5 of the supernova at once, but in the&nbsp;
end LUffy was really the one who did over 90% of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:45.000
the damage it took to take him down. So a bounty&nbsp;
higher than Teach makes sense. Now you could argue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.360
that Luffy deserves a bounty higher than Kaido&nbsp;
for taking him down. Instead of Kaido's 4Billion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.720
the much quoted 5,6Billion, go mu, in line&nbsp;
with luffy's gomu gomu no mi. Only that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:04.380
we now know that there actually is no GOmu GOmu no&nbsp;
mi. So I think that this particular wordplay might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:10.320
well be off the table now. The fact that taking&nbsp;
down both Kaido and Big Mom took a major team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:16.200
effort, in my opinion justifies a lower bounty&nbsp;
than them. Again, just because Teach took out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:22.560
WHitebeard, doesn't mean that he got a 6Billion&nbsp;
bounty afterwards. Luffy usually got a highter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.140
bounty than his opponent, because he took them out&nbsp;
at full strength. An antagonist like Katakuri for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:34.320
instance started at full health against Luffy. So&nbsp;
raising his bounty higher than theirs makes sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:40.080
at least from the outside perspective. Morgan and&nbsp;
the government didn't really know what was going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:47.040
on in the mirror world. However CP0 was reporting&nbsp;
every last detail about the raid to the outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:54.900
world. So the bounty could be adapted a lot more&nbsp;
precisely. On top of that, putting Luffy above&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:01.500
Kaido's level would also have put him above&nbsp;
Shanks, who has been a Yonko for much longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:08.520
than Luffy. I would assume that you would have to&nbsp;
repeatedly do crazy things like this, to actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:15.540
raise your bounty even further. Maybe Luffy will&nbsp;
overtake Shanks after they have actually met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.220
in the story, which would make a lot more sense&nbsp;
narrative wise as well I think. Then of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:28.980
the 3Billion bounty fits in incredibly nicely with&nbsp;
luffy's path so far. He went form a 30 Million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:36.000
Rookie bounty, to a 300 Million Warlord level&nbsp;
bounty to 1.5 Billion after defeating Katakuri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.880
in other words half a YOnko bounty. And now&nbsp;
he has officially entered the YOnko realm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:46.740
completing the 3 series with 3&nbsp;
Billion Berries on his flaming head.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:53.220
Then of course, there is the question why&nbsp;
both Law and Kid have gotten the same bounty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:59.160
as Luffy. Rightfully, you might say that Luffy&nbsp;
is the most powerful out of those 3. Now I was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.860
honestly pretty surprised about this reveal as&nbsp;
well. However I really really like it honestly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:11.160
Similarly to Luffy, both Law and Kid deserve&nbsp;
90% of the credit for taking down Big Mom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.220
And I think the government valued the act of&nbsp;
taking out a YOnko here and not just power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:23.280
scale everyone. Instead of splitting Luffy's&nbsp;
bounty and giving Law and Kid 1.5 Billion each,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:30.060
they were looking at the alliance of these 3&nbsp;
captains as a whole and want to see all 3 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:35.880
them captured for the threat they now pose. It&nbsp;
also really nicely, and honestly unexpectedly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:42.540
sets up Law and Kid as true rivals to Luffy&nbsp;
for finding the One PIece. It suddenly gives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:48.180
them a lot more relevance for the remaining&nbsp;
story than I would originally have suspected.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:53.640
Plus it gives Luffy the chance to distinguish&nbsp;
himself from the two even more in the future.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:59.280
Which is a really important point too I think,&nbsp;
that I'm actually pretty excited about. Giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:04.860
LUffy a mid-range Yonko bounty strongly&nbsp;
suggests to me that we will see at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:12.660
one more bounty poster for him at some point,&nbsp;
reaching the pinnacle of the pirate world. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.220
have to remember, that Luffy defeating the&nbsp;
world government will mean no more wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:23.700
posters. And so I speculated before, that&nbsp;
Wano might well be the last increase we see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:29.880
for all the straw hats. But no, it really&nbsp;
looks like we'll get at least one more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:37.260
Maybe after ELbaf or maybe even after Luffy&nbsp;
becomes the new pirate king, just like Roger.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:41.640
Now in case you're STILL salty about LUffy&nbsp;
having the same bounty as Kid and Law,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:47.640
I want to remind you, that the World Government&nbsp;
is very much aware of Luffy being the strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:54.720
out of the three. DOn't forget how much they&nbsp;
fear the return of the sun god Nika. And so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:01.500
I think they decided to not put that into his&nbsp;
bounty, but instead gave Luffy one of the now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:09.420
two open spots among the four emperors, while Law&nbsp;
and Kid don't get that title. Luffy being a YOnko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:15.600
is what really distinguishes him from the other&nbsp;
two. And if you don't believe me, just look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:22.260
Kid's reaction this chapter. He thinks exactly&nbsp;
the same. Of course he's just joking, I think,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:26.700
when he says that he now has come for Luffy's&nbsp;
head, but he very much understands that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:33.240
government sees Luffy above him and Law. So&nbsp;
overall I do genuinely believe that the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:39.720
bounties are pretty much perfect, especially&nbsp;
with Luffy now being officially a Yonko.

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:45.660
I actually really that we only got these 3&nbsp;
bounties and the new Yonko reveal this chapter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:51.060
don't worry we'll get to buggy. But yeah, the fact&nbsp;
that all the straw hats have gotten new bounties,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:57.960
but we will get those after the break is pretty&nbsp;
dope I think. That basically guarantees that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:03.780
will have a banger chapter right away after&nbsp;
the break and it also gives Oda an extra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:11.520
week of breathing time, because I assume&nbsp;
1054 will be at least 50% bounty posters.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:16.800
Now sadly, that won't include my&nbsp;
own wanted poster. Even though my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:26.100
own bounty has raised from 59M to&nbsp;
60M recently after we hit 600.000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:31.920
subscribers on the channel this week, because&nbsp;
every single subscriber equals 100 Berries on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.360
top of my bounty! Honestly, thank you so so&nbsp;
much for your support. It means the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:41.880
Especially since we have been at war with&nbsp;
this man here. Trebol, who still is almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:48.120
40M berries ahead of us. But we'Re coming&nbsp;
for you Trebol. We'll show you who's boss.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:55.920
What I once again found super interesting is&nbsp;
how Big News Morgan is once again disobeying the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:03.360
government censorship. While he got the official&nbsp;
bounties and the Yonko news from the gorosei,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:09.900
he decided to print an image of Luffy in gear&nbsp;
5 on his wanted poster, basically publishing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:17.220
LUffy's new godly appearance to the entire world.&nbsp;
A photo that CP0 managed to take during the fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:23.100
I guess in an effort to let the cylinder&nbsp;
guy's death not be in vain. Understandably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:28.860
the Gorosei are furious about this leak. The&nbsp;
government has tried to erase the true nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:38.040
the Nika fruit form history, and now its awakened&nbsp;
form will be seen in every single corner of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:44.100
world. This will be especially concerning, because&nbsp;
there are people out there who will know exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:50.220
what they are looking at. I'm thinking, Shanks,&nbsp;
Rayleigh, maybe also Blackbeard and Dragon. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:56.760
other words, having some of the most powerful&nbsp;
and dangerous people in the world find out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:04.980
joy boy has returned, will make things even more&nbsp;
unstable for the government than it already was.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:11.400
I actually also found it hilarious that apparently&nbsp;
the CP agents were taken out by Big Mom's ship.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:19.620
Hilarious, because they were completely useless&nbsp;
for the entirety of the raid, but also because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:26.280
it still makes me wonder wether Big Mom and&nbsp;
Kaido might not have survived somehow in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:33.180
end. And it also raises the question, what the&nbsp;
Big Mom pirates will do now that their leader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:38.040
has been taken out. The beast pirates&nbsp;
have all been decimated after the raid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:43.920
especially with Greenbulls arrival. But the&nbsp;
big mom pirates are basically still fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:49.440
functional in full force. Will Katakuri&nbsp;
become their new captain? And how will he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:54.480
react to Big Mom having been defeated? Will&nbsp;
he try to avenge her? Or join forces with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:10:01.980
Luffy? For some reason I haven't really thought&nbsp;
about this before, but now I'm super curious.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:10.200
And speaking of Greenbull: What the hell happened&nbsp;
there? It seems like King and Queen tried to fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:16.680
him and got completely decimated. Greenbull,&nbsp;
or Aramaki, as he's called, is an absolute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:22.800
monster. It turns out that he doesn't use his&nbsp;
plant powers for photosynthesis to survive, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:29.580
instead he literally sucks the life force out of&nbsp;
his opponents to heal himself. This devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:37.620
whatever it is, might be one of the, if not&nbsp;
the most terrifying power I have seen in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:45.120
entirety of the story. Like just imagine what&nbsp;
you could do with it. Build entire cities if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:52.260
wanted to. IT's basically the one piece version of&nbsp;
Hashirama. His abilities are basically perfect to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:58.980
take out a large amount of medium strong opponents&nbsp;
all at once. An incredibly precise, yet wide-range&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:05.400
attack. And on top of that he also seems to be a&nbsp;
swordsman, just like Issho, carrying what looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:14.220
to be a black blade. This once against makes me&nbsp;
wonder, if he's not actually someone from Wano.&nbsp;

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:17.820
Something else that might hint towards&nbsp;
that is his real life inspiration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.840
that people on the Internet were once again&nbsp;
super quick to find out. As you probably know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:30.300
all admirals are inspired by Japanese actors. And&nbsp;
Greenbull is no exception. He's the spiting image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:37.200
of Yoshio Harada, a super famous Japanese actor,&nbsp;
who was especially known for two types of roles:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:43.800
Rebells and Samurai. We can see the rebel&nbsp;
in him for constantly disobeying Akainu's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.960
orders and the Samurai think once again&nbsp;
might hint at a connection with Wano.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:55.080
Now I originally speculated, that&nbsp;
he might actually be a good guy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.080 --> 00:12:03.660
who similarly to Aokiji will sympathise with&nbsp;
Luffy's cause. However after seeing how brutal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:12.300
he is and how good he finds Akainu's extreme way&nbsp;
of doing things...I'm not so sure. He literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:18.360
says he's coming for Luffy's head. Now he might&nbsp;
still turn out to be a good guy or Zoro's father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:26.100
but it doesn't seem like it. Though honestly he&nbsp;
can be both, Zoro's father AND a bad guy. I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.660
a lot more thoughts about Greenbull, but I'll save&nbsp;
that for a whole video on him during the break.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:36.780
Meanwhile, we have the major celebration going&nbsp;
on in the flower capital. Basically seeing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:44.520
start of the big banquet we have all been waiting&nbsp;
for. The best thing about this is how it shows how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:51.420
much Luffy has grown throughout Wano and the New&nbsp;
World, while still being the very same person at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:57.600
heart we first fell in love with. He doesn't want&nbsp;
to take away from Momo's moment and he sees all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:04.740
the people of Wano eat and drink for free and as&nbsp;
much as they like, basically a mini version of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:16.440
dream that we got revealed just a few chapters&nbsp;
ago. It seems like becoming a Yonko and beating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:22.080
Kaido has made luffy a little bit wiser, as&nbsp;
weird as it may sound in regards to Luffy.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:31.380
But for some reason there is even more to this&nbsp;
chapter. Because in the secret basement, with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:38.160
dolls that we already had seen before, Robin, who&nbsp;
I'm happy to say has not been captured by anyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:44.040
yet, has a conversation with Hitetsu, one of&nbsp;
the first characters we ever saw in Wano. Well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:52.860
it turns out that he is actually Kozuki Sukiyaki,&nbsp;
Oden's father who we all had thought to be dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:58.620
for a long long time. This is such an interesting&nbsp;
reveal, because it opens up so many questions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:05.880
but since we barely get any answers here, I want&nbsp;
to move on to talking about Pluton. Robin. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:12.600
the heck. How did you know about Pluton being&nbsp;
in Wano since Alabasta and never mentioning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:18.420
it once? Not only does this once again underline&nbsp;
the fact that Alabasta seems to have been allied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:23.340
with the Ancient Kingdom in some way or form,&nbsp;
in this case specifically Wano, but it also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:32.160
begs the important question once again: What is&nbsp;
Pluton? Is there a giant battleship hidden in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:38.940
Wano? Or is it literally Momonosuke, just how&nbsp;
it was Shirahoshi on fishman island? I feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:45.840
like we might be getting some lore on the ancient&nbsp;
weapons in the story quite soon with this reveal.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:53.100
But let's move on to my personal and I guess your&nbsp;
personal highlight of this entire chapter. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:59.040
right here. Who would have thought, that&nbsp;
the cover of volume 25 would foreshadow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:06.420
the future 4 emperors of the sea for the 25th&nbsp;
anniversary of One Piece? Like rally Oda-sensei,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:18.060
just how much did you actually plan this story&nbsp;
in advance? Is this an actual coincidence? Buggy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:23.880
becoming an emperor of the sea is just the biggest&nbsp;
plot twist ever. It throws up so many questions:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:31.200
How did that happen? Is buggy actually&nbsp;
just lucky or is he a secret master&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:37.500
mind? Was Buggy the pirate that shanks was&nbsp;
talking about to the Gorosei to distract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:42.540
them from Luffy? I want to take my time and&nbsp;
discuss this in a whole video, but for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:47.220
if you really want to understand how the&nbsp;
world government thinks and functions and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:52.740
how the Gorosei rule the world, you should&nbsp;
not miss out on this video right here.

